--
-- "Every test is executed and its evidence returned with the build: test
--  identifier, actual result, pass or fail, build version, date,
--  tester."
--
-- Thirty records, one per test. Nine passed, fourteen are blocked by a
-- governing input that does not exist, and seven were not executed in
-- this run and say so.
--
-- §11: "Where a test cannot pass because a governing input is missing,
-- record it as a conflict — do not resolve it by hiding a field, adding
-- free text, introducing a default, combining controls, or reducing
-- either live view." The fourteen blocked records name the missing input
-- rather than a weakened version of the test.
--
-- The seven not-executed records are the ones it would have been easiest
-- to write a reason for and call passed. They are recorded as not
-- executed because they were not executed.
--
-- This does not make the acceptance evidence complete, and
-- t3a_d1_acceptance_evidence_complete() will keep returning false and
